\subsection{Cross-VLA Generalization}

\looseness=-1 The pipeline is VLA-agnostic by construction: the $K{=}2$ uncertainty probe, argmin-to-centroid selection, and bounded CRM correction depend only on the base policy producing diverse action samples and exposing an observation embedding. Across the three VLAs in Table~\ref{tab:main}, the CRM architecture, training recipe ($K{=}10$ forward passes on 40 LIBERO tasks), and threshold percentile are unchanged; only the input projection adapts to the VLA's observation dimensionality. Two questions guide the remaining evaluations. First, does correction help when the base policy is already strong? $\pi_{0.5}$ operates at $81.5{/}84.2$\% on Object/Spatial, leaving limited headroom and probing the bounded-residual mechanism outside the high-error regime where SmolVLA was developed. Second, does the gate degrade gracefully when sample diversity vanishes? OpenVLA-OFT at $T{=}0.5$ produces nearly identical samples across $K{=}2$, collapsing the probe and stress-testing the stochastic-diversity prerequisite. Per-VLA threshold sensitivity and the Goal/Long evaluations are reported in Appendix~\ref{sec:cross_vla}.

